   "cooked": "<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#proposal-title-1\" name=\"proposal-title-1\"></a><strong>Proposal title</strong>\n</h3>\n<p>Commons Upgrade Runoff Vote</p>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#tldr-2\" name=\"tldr-2\"></a>TL;DR</h3>\n<p>Here are the top 5 proposals chosen in the <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/voting-for-the-final-params-for-the-commons-upgrade/682/20\">Tokenlog curation phase.</a> They represent the favorite economic designs for the TEC. This runoff vote uses Quadratic Ranked Choice Voting to pick the final parameter set that will be used to upgrade the TEC into a fully functioning Commons with Conviction Voting, Tao Voting and Augmented Bonding Curve.</p>\n<p>Next step after this vote is to submit the winning proposal to the Hatch DAO for final implementation.</p>\n<p>We are approaching the launch of the <strong>Token Engineering Commons</strong> and <strong>$TEC.</strong> This is a collaboratively designed Commons economy.</p>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#proposal-description-3\" name=\"proposal-description-3\"></a>Proposal description</h3>\n<p><strong>1. <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/commons-upgrade-parameter-runoff-goldilocks-1-bet-for-1-mil-to-advance-token-engineering-127/778\">Goldilocks</a></strong><br/>\n<strong>2. <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/commons-upgrade-parameter-runoff-mathmematics-v4-back-to-the-square-roots-but-still-with-1-memillion-common-pool-138/780\">Mathmematics</a></strong><br/>\n<strong>3. <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/commons-upgrade-parameter-runoff-the-bolsheviks-gambit-fork-with-revolutionary-opening-price-and-iron-curtain-conviction-voting-109/779\">Bolsheviks Gambit</a></strong><br/>\n<strong>4. <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/vote-for-ostroms-1-million-dollar-baby-for-tec-commons-config-84/740\">Ostrom’s Baby</a></strong><br/>\n<strong>5.  <a href=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/t/4-20-public-open-meets-ostrom-s-1m-hatch-fledge-fly/760\">4.20</a></strong></p>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#additional-information-to-add-4\" name=\"additional-information-to-add-4\"></a>Additional information to add</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Voter Pamphlet</strong><br/>\n<a class=\"inline-onebox\" href=\"https://docs.google.com/presentation/d/1PlaxG-FZh0TJIjiM-gV6cgAzVgEaqNEyW4V-bgdC78Y/edit#slide=id.g10a24d77ef3_5_0\">Commons Upgrade Proposal - Google Präsentationen</a></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Debates</strong><br/>\n<strong>Friday</strong> , <strong>Jan. 7,</strong> 2:30 - 4pm EST / 8:30 - 10pm CET<br/>\n<strong>Monday</strong> , <strong>Jan. 10</strong>, 11am - 12:30pm EST / 5 - 6:30pm CET<br/>\n<strong>Tuesday</strong> <strong>, Jan. 11,</strong> 1pm - 2:30pm EST / 7 - 8:30pm CET<br/>\n<strong>Final debate! Wed., Jan. 12,</strong>  time tbd, check TEC <a href=\"https://calendar.google.com/calendar/u/0/embed?src=5mkep1ad1j860k6g7i7fr8plq0@group.calendar.google.com&amp;ctz=Europe/Berlin\">calendar.</a></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#how-does-this-proposal-benefit-the-community-andor-the-field-of-token-engineering-5\" name=\"how-does-this-proposal-benefit-the-community-andor-the-field-of-token-engineering-5\"></a>How does this proposal benefit the community and/or the field of Token Engineering?</h3>\n<p>The design of the TEC economy has been done collaboratively and inclusively.<br/>\nThe Commons Config Dashboard ante the Collaborative Economics process are a public good to the token engineering field.</p>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#how-will-these-funds-be-used-only-for-conviction-voting-6\" name=\"how-will-these-funds-be-used-only-for-conviction-voting-6\"></a>How will these funds be used? (Only for conviction voting)</h3>\n<p><em>Provide a breakdown for how funds will be used. Proposals requesting less funds have a higher chance to pass, consider breaking your proposal into milestones that can be submitted separately.</em></p>\n<h3>\n<a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#how-will-you-share-progress-7\" name=\"how-will-you-share-progress-7\"></a>How will you share progress?</h3>\n<p>The final result will be shared in this forum post and the winning proposal will be submitted to the Hatch DAO.</p>",
